WEBVTT

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.400
Del: Whatever’s inside these doors, those bugs don’t like it.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.200
Del: There's nothing on this thing. How am I supposed to open it?

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:13.600
Luke: With the key.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.340
Del: Why would the Emperor have a vault that can only be opened using the Force?

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:26.720
Luke: Why do you think?

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.760
Del: You're telling me the man who destroyed the Jedi Order is secretly one of them?

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.900
Luke: No. I'm telling you that as a boy on Coruscant you were frightened of the wrong thing.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.600
Del: There's nothing dangerous in here. The Emperor is protecting junk.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.120
Del: This is all worthless.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:01.000
Luke: Not all of it.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:07.260
Del: What is that?

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:11.220
Luke: I'd like to keep this compass, if you don't mind.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.660
Del: My mission is to destroy this place. Why would I let you do that?

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:15.560
Luke: Because I asked.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:20.280
Luke: Thank you.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:29.340
Luke: I won’t stop you from destroying this vault. But wouldn’t you say the Empire has done enough damage to innocent worlds?

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.800
Luke: I'm glad we were brought together, Del.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:48.360
Del: So, what happens now? We both walk off in separate directions and pretend like this never happened?

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:53.160
Luke: I don't think you can. There's still conflict in you.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:02:01.560
Del: Of course there's conflict in me. I'm not blind. I know what the Empire's capable of. But what else is there?

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:02.940
Luke: A choice.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:05.560
Del: The Rebellion?

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:08.320
Luke: No. A choice to be better.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.120
Luke: May the Force be with you.
